  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "ch1",
      "title": "Chapter 1: The Sound",
      "pages": [
        {
          "number": 1,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "The sun was going down on Willowbrook Hollow. The sky was pink and gold.",
            "Moss the hedgehog sat by the stream. He was having a snack of bugs. It was calm and still.",
            "Then a sound came from the barn.",
            "SKREEE-AWK!",
            "Moss dropped his bug. His spines stood up. He rolled into a ball."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "SKREEE-AWK! SKRONK!",
            "The sound went up. It went down. It went up again.",
            "Moss peeked out of his ball. The barn was part of the sanctuary. That was where the giant came each day to help the critters.",
            "“Something is in the barn,” Moss said softly. “Something big. Something bad.”",
            "Then he rolled up again, just to be safe."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/brindle_master.png",
              "alt": "Brindle the old dog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "pulse",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "Moss ran to find Brindle. The old dog was asleep under the big oak tree. His green bandana was over one eye.",
            "“Brindle! Wake up!” said Moss. “There is a monster in the barn!”",
            "Brindle did not open his eyes. “Is it a big monster?” he asked.",
            "“It is a LOUD monster,” said Moss.",
            "“Then it will still be loud in the morning,” said Brindle. And he went back to sleep."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/brindle_master.png",
              "alt": "Brindle the old dog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "pulse",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch2",
      "title": "Chapter 2: Wren Has News",
      "pages": [
        {
          "number": 4,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "The next morning, Wren flew down from the oak tree. She landed on a stump with a thump.",
            "“News! News! Big news!” she sang. “I know what is in the barn!”",
            "The whole Hollow came to hear. Tansy the squirrel ran down a tree. Pip and Pebble ran out of a log.",
            "Moss came too. He came very, very slowly."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/wren_master.png",
              "alt": "Wren the songbird",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "“I was on the barn roof,” said Wren. “The giant was there. She had a big black box.”",
            "Wren puffed up her chest. “The giant said, ‘I have to practice my viola.’” Then she said it again, louder. “A VI-O-LA!”",
            "“What is a viola?” asked Moss.",
            "Wren did not know. But Wren never let that stop her."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/wren_master.png",
              "alt": "Wren the songbird",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/zoe_master.png",
              "alt": "Zoe, the giant helper",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "“A vi-o-LA,” said Wren, slower. “Vi-o-LION. It is a LION! The giant keeps a lion in a box!”",
            "The Hollow gasped.",
            "Pip fell off the log. Pebble fell on Pip.",
            "Just then, Leo strolled up. His mane was full of grass. He held his wish ball in one paw."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/wren_master.png",
              "alt": "Wren the songbird",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/pip_pebble_master.png",
              "alt": "Pip and Pebble, the mouse twins",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 7,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "“Did I hear the word lion?” asked Leo.",
            "“I am the only lion in this Hollow,” he said. “And I eat grass.” He took a big, loud munch to show them.",
            "“Maybe it is a very small lion,” said Wren. “With a very big roar.”",
            "Leo looked at his wish ball. It did not glow. “Hmm,” said Leo. “I do not think so.”"
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/leo_master.png",
              "alt": "Leo the lion holding his wish ball",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch3",
      "title": "Chapter 3: Tansy Has a Plan",
      "pages": [
        {
          "number": 8,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "Tansy hopped up on a rock. “I have a plan!” she said. “It has eleven steps!”",
            "“Step one: we sneak up to the barn. Step two: we hide in the hay.”",
            "“Step three: Pip and Pebble go up on the shelf. Step four: Wren sings a song. Step five: the lion gets sleepy.”"
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/tansy_master.png",
              "alt": "Tansy the squirrel",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 9,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "“Why do WE go up on the shelf?” asked Pip.",
            "“Why not YOU?” asked Pebble.",
            "“Because you are small,” said Tansy. “Step six: we open the box. Step seven: we give the lion a nice snack of grass.”",
            "“There is no lion,” said Leo. “I am the lion.”",
            "“And then,” said Tansy. “And then… um…”"
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/tansy_master.png",
              "alt": "Tansy the squirrel",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/pip_pebble_master.png",
              "alt": "Pip and Pebble, the mouse twins",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 10,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "Tansy stopped. She forgot what came next. Then she forgot step one. She forgot all of the steps!",
            "Brindle the old dog lay in the shade. He had one eye open. He had been asleep for steps two to six.",
            "“That is a lot of steps,” said Brindle. “Maybe we just go and look.”",
            "Moss did not want to go and look. Moss wanted to be a ball."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/brindle_master.png",
              "alt": "Brindle the old dog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "pulse",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch4",
      "title": "Chapter 4: Into the Barn",
      "pages": [
        {
          "number": 11,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "At dusk, the Hollow went to sneak up on the barn. Tansy went first, on her tiptoes.",
            "“Shh,” said Tansy. “We are as still as a moth. We are as still as a rock.”",
            "Then Moss stepped on a stick. SNAP!",
            "Moss rolled into a ball. The ball rolled down the hill. It rolled past Pip. It rolled past Pebble. It went BUMP into Leo’s leg.",
            "“Hello, Moss,” said Leo. He gave the ball a gentle push back up the hill."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/leo_master.png",
              "alt": "Leo the lion holding his wish ball",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 12,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "At last, the Hollow got to the barn. Tansy went first. Moss went last. Very, very last.",
            "The barn door was shut. A big latch held it closed.",
            "“Step one,” said Tansy. “We… um. How do we get in?”",
            "No one had a plan for the door."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/tansy_master.png",
              "alt": "Tansy the squirrel",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 13,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "Click. The latch swung up. The door creaked open.",
            "Echo the fox sat on the step. He did not look at the latch. He did not look at them. He just licked his paw.",
            "“That door was open the whole time,” said Echo.",
            "It was not. But Echo liked to help in secret."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/echo_master.png",
              "alt": "Echo the fox with his green satchel",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 14,
          "layout": "art-full",
          "text": [
            "In the barn, it was dim. It smelled like hay and goats.",
            "Puddle the duck waddled in. He was not looking for a lion. He was looking at a moth.",
            "The moth landed on the black box. Puddle went after the moth. He bumped the box with his bill.",
            "The box fell open with a POP!"
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/puddle_master.png",
              "alt": "Puddle the duck",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 15,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "There was no lion in the box. There was a thing made of wood. It had a long neck and four thin strings. Next to it was a long stick.",
            "“Is THAT the monster?” asked Moss.",
            "“It is a very thin lion,” said Wren.",
            "Then they heard boots. Clomp, clomp, clomp. The giant was coming! The Hollow dove into the hay."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/wren_master.png",
              "alt": "Wren the songbird",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch5",
      "title": "Chapter 5: Squeaks and Songs",
      "pages": [
        {
          "number": 16,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "The giant was Zoe. She had on red boots and a green dress. Under the dress she had on striped pants.",
            "Zoe picked up the viola. She set it under her chin. She pulled the bow across the strings.",
            "SKREEE-AWK!",
            "Moss rolled into a ball.",
            "Zoe did not give up. She played the same notes again, but slower."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/zoe_master.png",
              "alt": "Zoe, the giant helper",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 17,
          "layout": "art-right",
          "text": [
            "Skree… awk.",
            "And again. And again. And again.",
            "Each time, the sound got a bit less squeaky. Each time, it got a bit more smooth.",
            "Moss peeked out of his ball. The sound was not so bad now. It was… kind of nice."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/zoe_master.png",
              "alt": "Zoe, the giant helper",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 18,
          "layout": "art-left",
          "text": [
            "Each day that week, the Hollow came back to the barn.",
            "Each day, Zoe did her practice. The squeaks got smaller. The song got bigger.",
            "On the last day, Zoe played a whole song. It was slow and sweet.",
            "Wren did not say one word. For once, Wren had no news. She just sat with her eyes shut.",
            "Leo’s wish ball began to glow blue."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/leo_master.png",
              "alt": "Leo the lion holding his wish ball",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "float",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/brindle_master.png",
              "alt": "Brindle the old dog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "pulse",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": 19,
          "layout": "art-full",
          "text": [
            "“How did the monster turn into music?” asked Moss.",
            "Brindle smiled. “Practice,” he said. “Squeaks turn into songs if you keep going.”",
            "Then Moss did something new. He did not roll into a ball. He sat up tall and hummed along.",
            "Puddle clapped his wings. He clapped off the beat. No one minded one bit."
          ],
          "media": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/moss_master.png",
              "alt": "Moss the hedgehog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "roll",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/brindle_master.png",
              "alt": "Brindle the old dog",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "pulse",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "images/characters/master/puddle_master.png",
              "alt": "Puddle the duck",
              "animation": {
                "kind": "wiggle",
                "trigger": "tap"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
